<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>{{ meta.title }}</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; margin: 2rem; color: #222; }
    h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
    h2 { margin-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid #ccc; padding-top: 1rem; }
    h3 { margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
    .meta, .limitations { color: #555; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .chart { margin: 0.8rem 0; }
    .verdict { font-weight: 700; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>{{ meta.title }}</h1>
  <p class="meta">
    Generated {{ generated_at }} · Snapshot SHA256 {{ meta.snapshot_sha256 }} ·
    {{ meta.n_draws }} draws across {{ meta.n_eras }} eras.
  </p>

  {% for era in eras %}
  <section>
    <h2>{{ era.name }}</h2>
    <p class="verdict">{{ era.headline }}</p>
    {% for family in era.families %}
    <section>
      <h3>{{ family.title }}</h3>
      <div class="chart">{{ family.svg | safe }}</div>
      <p>{{ family.intuition }}</p>
      <p>{{ family.verdict }} {{ family.chance }}</p>
    </section>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  <section>
    <h2>Power analysis</h2>
    {% if power_svg %}
    <div class="chart">{{ power_svg | safe }}</div>
    {% else %}
    <p>No power-analysis grid was supplied.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <p>This shows how often the planted test biases were detected, so a quiet report is meaningful only where the tests are powerful.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="limitations">
    <h2>Limitations</h2>
    <p>This audit tests the recorded draw data, not the physical machine. A pass means these checks found no convincing deviation in this snapshot; it is not a guarantee of future fairness.</p>
  </section>
</body>
</html>
